{"slug":"unique-sorted-array","title":"Remove Duplicates from a Sorted Array","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"easy","order":105,"tags":["arrays","two-pointers","sorted"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Equal neighbours in a sorted array","body":["In a sorted array all copies of a value stand next to each other. So a value is a duplicate exactly when it equals the element just before it, and one pass comparing neighbours finds all the distinct values.",{"code":"unique = [a[0]]\nfor i in range(1, n):\n    if a[i] != a[i - 1]:\n        unique.append(a[i])"},"Without the sorted order you would need extra memory (a set) to remember what you have seen. The order saves that memory."]},"statement":["You are given an array of `n` integers sorted in non-decreasing order. Print the number of distinct values, and then the distinct values in order."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`.","The second line has `n` integers in non-decreasing order."],"outputFormat":["The first line: the number of distinct values `d`.","The second line: the `d` distinct values."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","-10^9 <= each number <= 10^9"],"examples":[{"input":"7\n1 1 2 2 2 5 7\n","output":"4\n1 2 5 7\n","note":"The distinct values are 1 2 5 7."}],"hints":["Equal values stand next to each other.","A value is new when it differs from the value before it.","The first element is always new."],"starter":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["In a sorted array, a value is new exactly when it differs from its left neighbour. Collect those values."],"complexity":"Time O(n), space O(n) for the output.","code":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nunique = [a[0]]\nfor i in range(1, n):\n    if a[i] != a[i - 1]:\n        unique.append(a[i])\nprint(len(unique))\nprint(*unique)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    vector<long long> unique = {a[0]};\n    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n        if (a[i] != a[i - 1]) unique.push_back(a[i]);\n    }\n    cout << unique.size() << \"\\n\";\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < unique.size(); i++) cout << unique[i] << (i + 1 < unique.size() ? \" \" : \"\\n\");\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        List<Long> unique = new ArrayList<>();\n        unique.add(a[0]);\n        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n            if (a[i] != a[i - 1]) unique.add(a[i]);\n        }\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < unique.size(); i++) sb.append(unique.get(i)).append(i + 1 < unique.size() ? \" \" : \"\\n\");\n        System.out.println(unique.size());\n        System.out.print(sb);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"7\n1 1 2 2 2 5 7\n","output":"4\n1 2 5 7\n"},{"input":"1\n3\n","output":"1\n3\n"},{"input":"4\n8 8 8 8\n","output":"1\n8\n"},{"input":"4\n1 2 3 4\n","output":"4\n1 2 3 4\n"},{"input":"5\n-5 -5 0 0 0\n","output":"2\n-5 0\n"},{"input":"30\n0 0 0 1 1 1 1 1 2 2 